From 9efe1f09fd505ce14defec59f6dfbcee092723f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 21:52:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0221 -- ORGCACHE-AUTO: auto-precache first launch +
 cold-render overlay

The organya backend cold-renders each .org -> PCM at song-start via a blocking
single-CPU synth pass (~57 s for the title song on a 486 DX2-66). On the target
that shows as a black screen / pegged CPU before the title menu -- the apparent
"hang". The fix machinery (per-song disk cache 0208, render-window quiesce 0214,
the host-side DOSKUTSU_ORG_PRECACHE_ALL batch + tier-scoped cache 0215) existed
but the cache was never populated ON the target, so every song still cold-rendered
once. The host/dist cannot pre-populate it: the PCM is Cave-Story-derived (not
redistributable) and build-sha + tier keyed.

This makes the SHIPPED game populate the cache itself, with feedback:

A. AUTO-PRECACHE ON FIRST LAUNCH -- after SoundManager::init (renderer up + font
   loaded, backend + tier resolved), if organya is the active backend and this
   binary/tier's cache is not marked complete (no CACHE\<rate>_<channels>\READY.OK
   sentinel whose stored sha matches this build), render ALL songs to the cache
   behind a one-time progress screen, then write the sentinel. Subsequent boots
   find the sentinel and skip straight to the title. ESC skips: abort the
   in-flight render (partial discarded -- the _org_cache_store empty-buffer guard
   prevents a truncated cache), stop the batch, write NO sentinel; the remaining
   songs cold-render on demand behind overlay B and the batch resumes next launch.

B. IN-GAME COLD-RENDER OVERLAY -- the SAME progress bar on ANY individual
   cold-render (a cache miss: an uncached / stale / changed-data song that slips
   past the sentinel and misses the per-song header validation), so a miss is
   never again a silent black screen.

Both share one mechanism: a per-beat callback (int return; nonzero = abort)
threaded into _org_render_song's synth loop, NULL by default. main.cpp registers
it ONLY after the headless host-batch block (which return 0s/exits first), so
DOSKUTSU_ORG_PRECACHE_ALL renders with cb==NULL -> byte-identical to 0215. Organya
stays decoupled from the Renderer (it only knows the function pointer); the
progress UI (clearScreen + headline + coarse "song N/M" bar + intra-song bar,
pixel-throttled flips, ESC poll) lives in main.cpp via the showLoadingScreen idiom.

The sentinel is a fixed 8.3 name CACHE\<rate>_<channels>\READY.OK whose CONTENT is
the full DOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12; the build key is in the content, NOT the filename.
g2k is MS-DOS 6.22 (no LFN) and plain 8.3 FAT truncates an extension to 3 chars,
so keying the sha in the name (READY.<sha>) would collapse it to 3 hex on disk (a
~1/4096 cross-build false-match -> skipped batch -> silent degrade of the
all-upfront choice to lazy in-game renders). present() reads the stored sha and
strncmp's it vs this binary's DOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12 (not a mere fopen-exists), so a
stale old-build sentinel is rejected and a fresh batch runs.

Organya-only (g_p10_audio_backend_active == AudioBackend::organya): OPL3/WB
dispatch to their chip in real-time and never cold-render, so a default install
never engages. Mono-only batch (mirrors precacheAllOrgs' stereo guard -- the
pre-render path is mono; a stereo tier is skipped, no sentinel). Default-ON
killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ORG_AUTOCACHE=0 disables both A and B (reverts to the
v1.1.0 black-screen cold-render). Single lever / own binary. Documented in
docs/internal/BOOT.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
